{"id":"cd1b4dafb5eb0840","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-isometry.md","title":"Isometry","display":"df-isometry — Isometry","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-isometry","aliases":["58-df-isometry","Isometry"],"display":"df-isometry — Isometry","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-isometry"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-isometry</span><span>Isometry</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-isometry — Isometry"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F,X,Y,d_X,d_Y\\in V\">\\(F,X,Y,d_X,d_Y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\)</span> (metric-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Isometry}_S\\subseteq V^5\\cup V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S\\subseteq V^5\\cup V^3\\)</span> (precise predicate and compatibility projection defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d_X)\\land\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(Y,d_Y)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,X,Y)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl(d_Y(F(x),F(y))=d_X(x,y)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d_X)\\land\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(Y,d_Y)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,X,Y)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl(d_Y(F(x),F(y))=d_X(x,y)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry\\text{-}compatibility} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,Y)\\leftrightarrow\\exists d_X,d_Y\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry\\text{-}compatibility} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,Y)\\leftrightarrow\\exists d_X,d_Y\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The five-argument core retains both metrics; the three-argument compatibility form existentially projects exactly those omitted structures.</li>\n<li>Isometry: distance-preserving map.</li>\n<li>The Hilbert-space identity <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|Ux\\|=\\|x\\|\">\\(\\|Ux\\|=\\|x\\|\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U^*U=I\">\\(U^*U=I\\)</span> are specialized consequences.</li>\n<li>Mazur-Ulam: surjective isometry between normed spaces is affine</li>\n<li>Banach: isometric embedding</li>\n<li>In Hilbert space: partial isometry generalizes unitary</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Munkres, Topology</li>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S$ (metric-space predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (function predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F,X,Y,d_X,d_Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Isometry}_S\\subseteq V^5\\cup V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d_X)\\land\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(Y,d_Y)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,X,Y)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl(d_Y(F(x),F(y))=d_X(x,y)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isometry\\text{-}compatibility} \\vdash \\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,Y)\\leftrightarrow\\exists d_X,d_Y\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(F,X,d_X,Y,d_Y)","display":true},{"tex":"\\|Ux\\|=\\|x\\|","display":false},{"tex":"U^*U=I","display":false}],"bytes":1519,"backlinks":[{"id":"93df685cc0032d09","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-706","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-isometry.md|58-df-isometry]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["ce876585d129ce97","36d7463d215be751"]}